                "**The Côte de Beaune** (south): Ladoix, Aloxe-Corton, Pernand-Vergelesses, Savigny-lès-Beaune, Beaune, Pommard, Volnay, Monthélie, Auxey-Duresses, Meursault, Puligny-Montrachet, Chassagne-Montrachet, Santenay. Also the kingdom of Chardonnay (Meursault, Montrachet).",
                "Beyond, two other regions complete the picture: Chablis (60 km northwest) and the Mâconnais (south), though their Climats classification is more rare.",
                "## How to visit the Climats",
                "**Interpretation centres:** the International City of Gastronomy and Wine (Dijon) and the Cité des Climats et Vins de Bourgogne (Beaune, opened 2023) are the best introductions. Allow 2-3h each.",
                "**Vineyard trails:** the Grands Crus Route (D974) links Dijon to Beaune through the villages. But the best is to leave it for the \"Climats trails\" — signposted footpaths through the plots. The Gevrey-Chambertin Climats trail (4 km) is a gem.",
                "**Domaine tastings:** book ahead. Our tip: don't try to visit three domaines in one day. One, two max — otherwise you lose the finesse. Choose a modest domaine over a prestigious one: the welcome is often more authentic.",
